course: dictionary
lesson: 8332
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Roma is one of them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer wants, and a capital letter is a clue too.
explain: «The Roma have lived in Europe for about a thousand years.» Here Roma means a people. Lived and Europe tell you it is about people, not a place or a food. The Roma are a people who have kept their own history and their own language, Romani.
explain: «Roma tomatoes are perfect for a rich pasta sauce.» Here a roma is a long, egg-shaped tomato. The word is about food, so the clue is in the sauce. When you read Roma, always ask: who, what or where is this about?
fact: Roma can mean a people, a name, or a type of tomato.
fact: The Roma are a people who have lived in Europe for about a thousand years. Their language is called Romani.
fact: Some people use the word Gypsy, but it can hurt. Roma or Romani is the respectful name.
fact: «Roma» is the Italian name for the city of Rome, the capital of Italy.
fact: A roma is a plum tomato: long, egg-shaped, and good for sauces. It is a noun, just like the people and the name.
exercise: «The Roma have lived in Europe for about a thousand years.» In this sentence, what does Roma mean? | A city in Italy | *A people who have lived in Europe for a long time | A tomato grown for sauce | A football club
exercise: Ella buys roma tomatoes for her sauce. What is a roma? | A purple plum | A people from northern India | *A long, egg-shaped tomato, good for sauces | A capital city
exercise: «Roma is the Italian name for Rome, the capital of Italy.» What does Roma mean here? | A kind of bread | A people in Europe | A plum tomato | *A city, the capital of Italy
test: Which of these is the name of the language many Roma speak? | Rome | Roma | Italian | *Romani
test: Which clue tells you Roma means a city? | The sentence is about cooking dinner | The sentence has a small r | The sentence is a question | *The sentence talks about Italy and the Italian name for Rome
exam: Which sentence shows that Roma means a people, not a tomato? | Roma is a small, round fruit. | *«The Roma have lived in Europe for about a thousand years.» | A roma is a long, red vegetable. | Ella cooked a sauce with roma tomatoes.
